(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[16 1 "// Finalization (PYS9 (a); doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"): pyi has no reference counts, so an object's"] [17 1 "// death is Go's collector's finding. A tracked object (one with weak references, or with a finalizer's work due: a"] [18 1 "// class's __del__, a generator's close, a socket's warning) has a Go finalizer and a record in tracked, keyed by its"] [19 1 "// address and never holding it. Go's finalizer goroutine only moves the dead object into finQueue and sets the eval"] [20 1 "// breaker's bit; the thread holding the GIL drains the queue (handleEvalBreaker, gc.collect). The order is reference"] [21 1 "// counting's (subtype_dealloc): the work first, the Go finalizer set again without it (PEP 442: once only); found"] [22 1 "// unreachable again, the weak references are cleared (in the Go finalizer, under finMu, so no weak reference yields"] [23 1 "// the object after it) and their callbacks called in CPython's list order. Go's heap does not move and an object with"] [24 1 "// a finalizer is kept until the finalizer ran, so a weak reference's hidden address is valid while it is not cleared."] [26 1 "// the work a tracked object's death runs"] [28 23 "// its class's __del__ (slot_tp_finalize)"] [29 23 "// a generator's, coroutine's or async generator's finalization (_PyGen_Finalize)"] [30 23 "// an open socket's ResourceWarning and close (sock_finalize)"] [31 23 "// an async generator's awaitable never awaited (async_gen_asend_finalize)"] [32 23 "// a built-in type's tp_finalize, the record's fin (TrackFinalizer, queue 241)"] [35 1 "// finTrack is a tracked object's record."] [37 21 "// the object's pointer's element type, to rebuild it from its address"] [38 21 "// its weak references in CPython's order: the basic ref, the basic proxy, then the newest first"] [39 21 "// the work due at its death"] [40 21 "// its identity once hashed (identityHash; an instance keeps it in its own field)"] [41 2 "// aioTask: a registered asyncio task past the strong list (builtins_asyncio.go's registry, queue 224)"] [43 2 "// owner is the interpreter that tracked it (queue 230): its work runs there, nil for the main one before any thread"] [45 2 "// fin is a built-in type's tp_finalize (workFin; queue 241), given the object: it must hold no reference to it"] [47 2 "// seq is the record's order of making (queue 253): a collection's trash is finalized in it, as CPython's lists"] [48 2 "// keep their objects in the order they were tracked"] [52 1 "// finSeq numbers the records (finMu)."] [55 1 "// finItem is a dead object's turn in the queue: obj and its work, or (obj nil) its weak references' callbacks."] [62 24 "// tracked, finQueue, the weak references' addresses (Go's finalizer goroutine takes it too)"] [65 26 "// the Go finalizers run so far (gc.collect waits until it stays still)"] [66 26 "// a drain is running (under the GIL): a nested one leaves the queue to it"] [68 18 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: nothing tracked (the weak references hold their referents, as before 218)"] [73 1 "// The moment at del (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): DELETE_FAST of a tracked object with work"] [74 1 "// or weak references due asks Go's collector at once whether that was the last reference, and drains the queue before"] [75 1 "// the next instruction: reference counting's moment when it was, a wasted collection when it was not. The collections'"] [76 1 "// time is held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time (and 50 ms); past it the death waits for the next collection."] [82 1 "// finDeletedAt is DELETE_FAST of f's fast local i (not unbound) with the check of the value it deletes. The value is"] [83 1 "// read and cleared here and dropped before anything else runs: no other variable, and no frame of a call goi"] [84 1 "// interprets, keeps it (goi's registers keep a returned call's values: queue 218's REQUEST), so that the collection"] [85 1 "// can find it dead."] [103 1 "// finPeek is the address of the value of name in d, before DELETE_NAME or DELETE_GLOBAL deletes it (0: nothing to"] [104 1 "// check); the deletion's moment is then finDeleted's, as DELETE_FAST's (queue 224: `del g` at a module's level)."] [120 1 "// finAddr is o's address for finDeleted when its holder lets it go (0: nothing to check); queue 293: sys.settrace's and"] [121 1 "// sys.setprofile's previous function, the thread's only reference to it, whose __del__ CPython runs as the call"] [122 1 "// drops it (test_sys_settrace's test_reentrancy: a __del__ that sets the trace function)."] [134 1 "// finDeleted is the check of a deleted object at address a."] [149 1 "// finVerify is the collection at a deletion: rounds while the object's record moves (its work run, then its weak"] [150 1 "// references cleared: subtype_dealloc's two steps), each a Go collection and a wait until the record moved or Go's"] [151 1 "// finalizers are still, then the drain."] [186 1 "// finQueued is whether tr's object is in the queue (finMu held)."] [196 1 "// addrOf is o's address (o a pointer: finTrackable)."] [199 1 "// hiddenPtr reads the address *u as a pointer (a weak reference's referent, alive while not cleared)."] [202 1 "// toObject is the object of type *elem at the address *u (a weak reference's referent; finMu held, *u not 0)."] [207 1 "// finTrackable is o's possible tracking: a pointer to a non-empty type of this package (another package's objects"] [208 1 "// may have their own Go finalizer, which a second SetFinalizer would abort on: _bz2's, _sqlite3's, _zstd's)."] [217 1 "// trackLocked is o's record, made (with its Go finalizer) when o has none; finMu held."] [236 1 "// trackWork tracks o (finTrackable) with the work w due at its death."] [247 1 "// TrackFinalizer is a built-in type's tp_finalize (queue 241): fin(o) runs under the GIL at o's death, once, in"] [248 1 "// __del__'s place in the order (a cycle's too). o is a pointer to a non-empty type with no Go finalizer of its own (a"] [249 1 "// type of another package may be given: pysqlite3's cursor); fin takes o as its argument and must hold no reference"] [250 1 "// to it (the record would keep it alive)."] [267 1 "// goFinalized is the Go finalizer of every tracked object, run on Go's finalizer goroutine: o into the queue."] [293 1 "// drainFinalizers runs the queue under the GIL until it is empty: the number of dead objects handled."] [320 4 "// its interpreter ended: no one to run the work in (queue 230)"] [345 2 "// the record stays (its Go finalizer set again) while weak references, new work or an identity need it"] [358 1 "// runWork runs the work w due at o's death (its record's work already cleared: PEP 442's once)."] [379 1 "// weakCallbacks calls the callbacks of a dead object's weak references, in its list's order (PyObject_ClearWeakRefs)."] [393 1 "// runDel is slot_tp_finalize: the class's __del__ called, its exception to sys.unraisablehook."] [404 1 "// finalizeGen is _PyGen_Finalize: an async generator with sys's finalizer hook handed to it; a coroutine never"] [405 1 "// started warns; a suspended generator or coroutine closed."] [425 1 "// warnUnawaitedCoroutine is _PyErr_WarnUnawaitedCoroutine: warnings._warn_unawaited_coroutine(coro), or a plain"] [426 1 "// RuntimeWarning when that failed other than by the warning itself."] [431 33 "// get_warnings_attr imports nothing at shutdown (queue 253)"] [458 1 "// finUnraisable is PyErr_FormatUnraisable from a finalizer (the object None)."] [465 1 "// finRound is one round of gc.collect: Go's collection, a wait until Go's finalizer goroutine has been still for a"] [466 1 "// moment (there is no public barrier), then the drain; the number of dead objects handled."] [483 1 "// finCollect is gc.collect's finalization: rounds until one handles nothing (at most 8), none when nothing is"] [484 1 "// tracked or queued; then the cycles through finalizers (cyCollect, queue 222) and the rounds again for what their"] [485 1 "// trash held; the number of cyclic trash nodes (CPython's count: acyclic garbage is reference counting's)."] [497 1 "// finRounds is 218's rounds: the dead objects handled."] [500 2 "// the classes' attribute caches out of date are dropped now, not at their next lookup: a stale answer (a method"] [501 2 "// deleted from its class) would keep its value alive"] [525 1 "// finalizeSocket is sock_finalize: an open socket warns ResourceWarning \"unclosed %R\" (its source the socket), then"] [526 1 "// its descriptor is closed."] [543 1 "// resourceWarn is PyErr_ResourceWarning(source, 1, msg): warnings.warn(msg, ResourceWarning, 1, source=source)."] [546 59 "// _warnings' own path at shutdown (queue 253)"] [560 1 "// growStack gives f's value stack room for n more values in a new array, the old one's values cleared: newFrame's one"] [561 1 "// allocation holds the fast locals and the stack's first array together, so the stack's stale values there would keep"] [562 1 "// their objects reachable through the fast locals for the frame's life (queue 218: found by a weak reference that a"] [563 1 "// function's first call did not clear)."] [572 1 "// pendingGens are the coroutines made, and the generators suspended in a try region, since the last flush (under the"] [573 1 "// GIL): one still not finished when the list is flushed (every 256, and in gc.collect) is tracked for its finalization,"] [574 1 "// so the common cases, a coroutine awaited at once and a generator run to its end, pay no Go finalizer (queue 218:"] [575 1 "// measured with bin/pyi aot, a coroutine 0.13 us untracked against 0.6 us tracked at creation; a generator with a"] [576 1 "// try 0.66 us against 1.0-1.2 us tracked at its first suspension)."] [587 1 "// track tracks a generator not finished for its finalization. Its frame's pointer back at it becomes an address: Go"] [588 1 "// never finalizes an object that reaches itself (queue 224: no suspended generator's frame let its generator die, so"] [589 1 "// neither close nor \"never awaited\" ran)."] [599 1 "// The moment at a call's return (queue 297; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 297\"): CPython's reference counting"] [600 1 "// frees a generator a call leaves suspended when the call drops its last reference (next(gen()), any(gen())): its"] [601 1 "// close then (GeneratorExit thrown in, finally blocks and a monitor's events), its frame's locals with it. pyi knows that"] [602 1 "// moment without a collection when the generator's only holder was the value stack: made by the calling frame's"] [603 1 "// previous instruction (stampGen: the frame's address and instruction, and callSeq, every call counting itself, so no"] [604 1 "// call ran between), not handed out since (f_generator marks it exposed), and the last argument of a consumer that"] [605 1 "// keeps no reference to its arguments (Builtin.dropsArg: next, any, all, min, max, sum, sorted). No instruction ran"] [606 1 "// between its making and the consumer's call, so nothing stored it; the consumer kept nothing; its own frame does not"] [607 1 "// hold it (a frame object does not keep its generator alive in CPython either). dropGen closes it at the return. Cost:"] [608 1 "// an increment per call and a flag test per built-in call; a collection only for its frame's locals with a finalizer"] [609 1 "// due (222's moment, as del's)."] [611 1 "// callSeq counts the calls (callStack, AotCallV, AotCallMethodV; queue 297)."] [614 1 "// stampGen stamps o, a generator just made by f's running instruction, with its making."] [621 1 "// freshGen is o when it is a generator not yet run, made by f's previous instruction with no call since (the call at"] [622 1 "// callSeq n0 the next one) and never handed out: held by the value stack alone, and now by the consumer's arguments."] [632 1 "// dropGen is the consumer's return for a fresh generator g: suspended, it dies now (_PyGen_Finalize: close, its error"] [633 1 "// to sys.unraisablehook), and its frame's locals with a finalizer due are checked at once (222's finDeleted)."] [635 62 "// exposed: f_generator handed out while it ran"] [640 20 "// a frame object handed out before the close (the close's own GeneratorExit traceback is dropped)"] [646 13 "// no frame object held elsewhere: its locals cleared, as _PyFrame_ClearExceptCode's"] [653 2 "// their collections held to a tenth of the wall time of their own (genSpent), apart from del's (finSpent)"] [662 1 "// genSpent is dropGen's collections' time (its locals' checks), held as finSpent is, apart from it."] [665 1 "// scrubSlots is n nested calls, each a window of 16 interface slots that goi clears at a call's entry: under stage 0's"] [666 1 "// goi a returned call's slots above the stack's top keep their values (the checkout's goi clears them since c9047d52),"] [667 1 "// here the closed frame's locals; compiled, nanoseconds."] [677 1 "// genLocalsDue are the addresses of the tracked objects with work or weak references due that f's fast locals and"] [678 1 "// cells hold (at most 4), read before f is dropped."] [707 1 "// generator is f's generator (f.f_generator), nil when none, or when it died first."] [734 1 "// Cycles through finalizers (queue 222; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\"): Go never frees a cycle that"] [735 1 "// reaches a finalized object from itself, so gc.collect() finds them as CPython's gc_collect_main does, with Go's"] [736 1 "// collector answering what deduce_unreachable's counts answer: which objects are held from outside. The graph's nodes"] [737 1 "// are instances (their dictionary, while not handed out as an object, and __slots__ folded in), lists, tuples and"] [738 1 "// dictionaries; its edges their slots of interface type that hold a node. Every edge between two probed nodes is"] [739 1 "// hidden (the slot set to nil, its target kept by address), each probed node given a probe's Go finalizer, and Go"] [740 1 "// collects with the GIL held: a node whose probe does not run is held from outside, and so is what it reaches."] [743 22 "// gc.DEBUG_SAVEALL"] [744 2 "// gcDebugUncollectable is gc.DEBUG_UNCOLLECTABLE (the shutdown's garbage list printed, queue 253)"] [746 33 "// a larger graph is left alone (Go's collection, 218's moment)"] [750 35 "// a probe's answer is being read (finMu): a probe that runs later only holds"] [751 35 "// the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu), held until the collection ends"] [752 35 "// those that ran after the answer was read"] [753 35 "// tracemalloc traced once: a list, a dict or a cell may carry its Go finalizer"] [754 35 "// gc.set_debug's flags"] [755 35 "// gc.garbage"] [756 2 "// gcCollecting: a gc.collect() runs (gc.collecting: faulthandler's \"Garbage-collecting\" line, queue 241)"] [760 1 "// cyNode is a node of the graph, never holding its object (its address is hidden from the collector)."] [764 18 "// its record when tracked"] [765 18 "// its slots that hold a node, by address: a slot in the node itself (a FutureIter's) must not hold it"] [766 18 "// in step: the slot is a typed pointer (*Dict, *Cell ...), else an Object"] [767 18 "// the nodes they hold, in step"] [774 1 "// cyLeaves are the objects a collection's graph does not walk (queue 241): the dictionaries of the modules sys.modules"] [775 1 "// holds and the builtins' (held from outside: walking them would walk the whole program), and the frames running on a"] [776 1 "// thread's stack (their slots change under the loop; their Go frames hold them). Set by cyCollect, nil otherwise."] [779 1 "// cySetLeaves computes cyLeaves for this collection."] [823 1 "// cyIsNode is whether o is a node: an object whose references cyTraverse lists (CPython's tp_traverse), not a leaf of"] [824 1 "// this collection (cyLeaves), and able to take a probe's Go finalizer (a list's, a dictionary's or a cell's Go finalizer"] [825 1 "// may be tracemalloc's once it traced: then none of them)."] [838 3 "// a frame a Python object may hold (a traceback's, f_back's, gi_frame's), not running on a thread's stack,"] [839 3 "// not of a generator (the generator's slots fold it in: 222's rule)"] [849 1 "// cyWalkable is a generator whose frame's slots can be hidden (queue 224): suspended, with no pointer from its frame"] [850 1 "// back at it (a generator that reaches itself never has a probe run), and its frame not handed out: what else holds"] [851 1 "// an escaped frame is not in the graph."] [856 1 "// cyAllRefs makes cyTraverse list every object a slot holds, not only nodes (the shutdown's walk, exitRefs: queue 253)."] [861 1 "// cyForced are the dictionaries an exit collection gives as dead (queue 253, pylifecycle.go): seeds of the graph,"] [862 1 "// probed, never held, an edge into one reaching nothing; cyForcedSeeds the same as objects; cyWeakAlive, when set,"] [863 1 "// tells whether a weak reference to the trash is outside it (its callback called)."] [870 1 "// cyVisit is cyTraverse's visitor: a slot of the node, its kind (typed: a pointer of a concrete type, else an Object)"] [871 1 "// and the node it holds."] [874 1 "// cyTraverse is tp_traverse (queue 241; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 241\"): f called with each slot of o (a"] [875 1 "// node) that holds a node. Only slots o owns alone are listed: a backing array shared with another holder would hide"] [876 1 "// that holder's reference. A reference the table does not list (a map's, a closure's, a field of a struct that is no"] [877 1 "// object) stays visible to Go's collector, which only keeps more alive."] [945 20 "// handed out as an object: a node of its own (queue 241)"] [952 31 "// _asyncio's Future or Task: the slots of a task's cycle (queue 224)"] [1069 1 "// cyGraph is the graph from the seeds (an object a probe would find held stays out of it), nil past cyMaxNodes."] [1115 1 "// cyRelevant is the nodes a probe must see: those of a strongly connected component with a cycle and a tracked node"] [1116 1 "// (Tarjan's, iterative), and what they reach. An acyclic dead object is Go's to find."] [1209 1 "// cyProbe asks Go's collector which of the nodes in are held from outside the set: the edges between them hidden, a"] [1210 1 "// probe's finalizer on each (a tracked node's own taken off), runtime.GC() with the GIL held, a wait until every"] [1211 1 "// probe ran or Go's finalizers are still; then the slots put back and the probes taken off. The answer: the nodes"] [1212 1 "// reachable (held from outside, or reached from such a node through the edges)."] [1232 2 "// with its probe set each node outlives its last reference: what an earlier probe held is let go now"] [1329 1 "// cyHideRegistries takes the probed nodes out of the runtime's registries that hold their keys where CPython holds"] [1330 1 "// nothing (queue 241, \"Design: 241\": the weak registries): id()'s identities of untracked objects and the functions'"] [1331 1 "// annotations. The returned function puts back the reachable nodes' entries once the answer is read; the trash's go"] [1332 1 "// (a tracked node's identity into its record), so that Go can free it."] [1366 22 "// the trash's identity in its record, should a finalizer resurrect it"] [1377 1 "// cyDebug (PYI_GC_DEBUG=1): each probe prints to stderr its nodes held from outside that no other probed node holds,"] [1378 1 "// the roots of what it keeps (queue 241: what to look at when a cycle is not found)."] [1413 1 "// cySetFinalizer gives n's object the probe's Go finalizer (a tracked node's own taken off first: Go allows one)."] [1422 1 "// cyRestore gives a surviving tracked node its own Go finalizer again (its record dropped when it needs none)."] [1439 1 "// cyClearWeakRefs clears the weak references to the trash's tracked nodes (handle_weakrefs): their callbacks, in each"] [1440 1 "// list's order, returned to be called once all are cleared (a weak reference is never a node: always \"outside\")."] [1452 24 "// a weak reference in the trash itself: no callback (handle_weakrefs)"] [1464 1 "// cyCollect is gc.collect()'s cycle detection: the trash found, PEP 442's order run over it; the number of trash nodes."] [1481 2 "// the trash in CPython's lists' order (cyOrder, queue 253): the finalizers and callbacks in a fixed order"] [1527 1 "// cySeq is a node's record's order, the untracked last."] [1535 1 "// cyCount is the probed nodes whose probe ran (finMu held)."] [1555 1 "// cyFind is the cyclic trash: from the tracked nodes (or, only given, from those nodes alone: the resurrection's"] [1556 1 "// check), the graph, its relevant part probed; every probed node restored but the trash's (they keep no Go finalizer)."] [1579 1 "// cyOrder is the trash in the order CPython's lists would hold it (queue 253): its collector moves what a container"] [1580 1 "// reaches behind the container, so the trash runs from what nothing else in it holds (the dead module dictionaries"] [1581 1 "// first, in sys.modules' order, then by the records' order) through the references in their slots' order, breadth"] [1582 1 "// first; a cycle nothing outside it holds starts at its oldest record. A wrapper is finalized before what it wraps"] [1583 1 "// (an unclosed text file flushes its buffer before its raw file closes)."] [1648 1 "// cySeedGraph builds the graph and its relevant part in a frame of its own, so no object of the walk stays in a live"] [1649 1 "// variable of the probe's caller."] [1690 3 "// a dead module dictionary and all it reaches are probed (queue 253)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[94 28] [114 28] [156 16] [156 27] [161 29] [161 56] [169 29] [219 21] [227 27] [271 21] [318 16] [367 29] [387 51] [399 42] [411 55] [420 24] [430 25] [441 64] [452 92] [460 25] [471 28] [471 55] [473 28] [509 16] [509 27] [532 51] [537 16] [545 25] [616 28] [681 12] [681 42] [685 40] [688 24] [715 21] [800 33] [813 19] [813 29] [880 13] [890 13] [895 13] [900 13] [905 13] [910 13] [915 13] [920 13] [925 13] [952 17] [977 26] [1050 18] [1076 21] [1080 23] [1